---
<BaseLayout
  title="Someone has to own the dashboard project | Alluvium"
  description="Dashboard projects stall when nobody owns scope, refresh, or who can see which rows. We run the work until the business uses the report."
  canonicalPath="/data-project-management-change-leadership"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold">
<article>
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/services">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Data Project Management</span></nav>
<p class="kicker">Data Project Management</p>
<h1>Someone has to own the dashboard project</h1>
<p class="lede">The work stalls when the file has no owner for the decisions that get it used. We run the project through to a report the business will open.</p>
<p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
</div></header>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The build can look done while finance still opens the old file</h2>
<p>Scope keeps moving after kickoff. The refresh has no owner, and neither does the question of who can see which rows. Training is a slide deck, and it happens after the meeting that needed the report.</p>
<p>Finance keeps the spreadsheet because nobody held those decisions long enough for the meeting to move.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The work happens in the report</h2>
<p>The people who have to use the number work in the report while there is still time to change it.</p>
